Attention all polypilers....here's the latest trick for tilting the
game lopsidedly in your favor:

SPOILERS

By now, you know how to make lotsa magic markers, and blank scrolls.
Once you've found the enchant weapon scroll, you can do the following:

  1) Make as many blesssed enchant weapon scrolls as you can.

  2) Group darts and arrows into a polypile, trying to get large
     clumps (e.g. 64 darts, 48 arrows, etc.).

  3) Polypile til you get a large clump of long swords in the pile.

  4) Drop everything else except a scroll of identify and go pick
     up the clump of long swords - you must be careful, because once
     the clump is broken (if you can't pick up the whole amount) it
     will not "re-clump".

  5) Identify the clump to get the "+" value.  Pick up a potion of holy
     water and bless the clump.  Standing over an enchant weapon scroll,
     drink a potion of booze or confusion, pick up the scroll and read it.
     This will "rustproof" the clump.

  6) If the clump is "+0" or +1", engrave "AB" until the clump is "-1".
     If it's already +2 you saved a scroll.  Now read blessed scrolls to
     make the clump, +2, +5, and then +8.

  7) Now divide the clump in fourths.  Try enchanting a clump, if you
     are successful (1 chance in 3), you'll have a +11 clump.  IF not,
     try the next pile.  If you get down to the last pile, divide it
     in fourths again.

  8) Keep going, whenever an enchantment is successful, divide the
     spoils and keep trying.

  9) At some point, you'll be down to a single +14, +17, +20, or
     maybe even a +23 long sword (blessed and rustproof), depending
     on how big a clump you started with.

 10) Dip the result in a fountain til it becomes Excalibur.  A +23
     Excalibur is an AWESOME weapon.

OK, now go win the game.  Then you can swear off polypiling and see if
you can still win next time.


